      "params": [],
      "data": {
        "text": "NATIVE GORGON BYTEBUS\nStart HydraPy Studio with --tracker.\nEnable automation and press Play.\nGorgon BUS -> Register -> Split/DAC.\n\nRequires GorgonBridge 2.2.0,\nByteBusLab 2.2.0 and VCV Free.\n\nRight-click Gorgon: BUS source.\nDefault Z: 0-1 becomes 00-FF.\nAlso Roll, Feedback, Hit mask.\nZ key n/255 programs byte n.\nHit mask: bits 0-3 = lanes 1-4;\nAIR counts, muted/zero vel do not.\n\nRegister SOURCE = Bus CLK.\nSplit outputs 1-8 are data bits;\noutput 9 is publication clock.\nBoth cables have 9 channels.\nBUS always uses 0/10 V, even in\nGorgon's ordinary 5 V CV profile.\n\nRegister BUS OUT can also drive\nLookup, Vastish BUS IN or OTIS\nFRAME BUS (FRM mode). OTIS still\nneeds separate pitch and gates.\n\nDAC output is (byte-128)*5/128 V.\nAudio devices are not configured."
      }
    }
